				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Restore static runtime environment configuration in Info.plist\n\nReintroduce the `LSEnvironment` dictionary into `Info.plist` containing critical bootstrap configuration required for the native backend to establish sidecar connections. This restores the static injection of gRPC ports (`NetworkMountainPort`, `NetworkCocoonPort`), product identifiers, and execution tier definitions (e.g., `TierRemoteProcedureCall`, `TierExtensionActivation`).\n\nThis reverses the recent removal of these static settings, as the current initialization logic depends on the `LSRuntimeEnvironment` dictionary for early-stage environment variable population before dynamic configuration sources are available. Retain the `CFBundleIconFile` entry to ensure correct icon resolution on macOS.",
			"SHA": "26d7f51e50a888a8aac54f47b665a380d01efc76"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T00:52:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove static runtime environment configuration from Info.plist\n\nStrip the `LSEnvironment` dictionary and associated `Disable` and `Trace` flags from `Info.plist`. These static configurations, which defined critical gRPC ports (`NetworkMountainPort`, `NetworkCocoonPort`) and execution tiers (e.g., `TierRemoteProcedureCall`, `TierExtensionActivation`), were re-introduced in the previous commit but are being removed to transition the runtime environment setup away from static plist injection.\n\nRetain the `CFBundleIconFile` entry to ensure the application icon is correctly resolved by macOS. This change prepares the native backend to source its runtime configuration exclusively from the `Mountain` environment variable system or dynamic initialization logic, reducing coupling with the application bundle's metadata and aligning with the flexible configuration strategy required for multi-platform deployment.",
			"SHA": "d29b58488ebff9a89e854038127b6ca2c6dadcb6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T00:14:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				15
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Restore experimental feature flags and runtime environment config\n\nReintroduce the `grove` and `cocoon` feature flags in `Cargo.toml` to enable conditional compilation for the future native extension host (Grove) and the current extension host sidecar (Cocoon). These flags are required by the build system's tier-gating logic.\n\nRestore the `LSEnvironment` dictionary in `Info.plist` containing critical runtime configuration values, including network ports for Mountain and Cocoon, product identifiers, and tier definitions (e.g., `TierRemoteProcedureCall`, `TierExtensionActivation`). This reverses the removal performed in previous commits, re-establishing the static environment injection required for the macOS application to bootstrap its sidecar connections.\n\nConcurrently, enhance documentation in the `Track/Effect/CreateEffectForRequest` module. Add comprehensive module-level comments and method tables to all RPC handler files (Documents, FileSystem, Git, LanguageFeatures, Languages, Search, StatusBar, TreeView, UserInterface, Webview, Workspace). These comments detail the specific RPC methods handled, the underlying `MountainEnvironment` trait providers used, and the execution model for each request type.",
			"SHA": "511f9b624577e1447543ef14f5d12723316a452c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T23:00:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Mountain): Enable experimental feature flags for terminals and debug protocol\n\nUpdate the default feature set in `Cargo.toml` to conditionally enable `terminals`, `debug-protocol`, `scm-support`, `child-processes`, and `Development` alongside existing `Cocoon`, `Mist`, and `Air` integrations. This consolidates the build configuration to activate support for terminal emulation, debugging capabilities, source control management, and child process handling by default.\n\nRemove the now-unused `grove` and `cocoon` feature placeholders from the list, aligning the feature registry with the current implementation status. This prepares the native backend for upcoming component integration while maintaining the explicit `Telemetry` and `Test` flags for optional toggling.",
			"SHA": "a2869e478f35c9bc90a23edc28e7a95f066f88a9"
		}
	],
